# Replace @your-org/vault-owners with the people or team who own this vault, then
# turn on "Require review from Code Owners" in the branch protection for main.
#
# An allowlist: every path needs an owner's review unless a later line frees it, because
# almost any new top-level path can be instructions or code for an agent or a tool
# (.claude/, .mcp.json, .obsidian/plugins/, .gitattributes, .venv, a new script). The last
# matching line wins, and a line with no owner frees its paths.
*                   @your-org/vault-owners
# Content a contributor edits in an ordinary change: pages, captures, and the generated
# root index. docs/plans/ stays owned: agents carry out plan files, so a plan is
# instructions.
/wiki/
/raw/
/index.md
# The vault's own rules and page templates are instructions every agent follows.
/wiki/system/       @your-org/vault-owners
/wiki/templates/    @your-org/vault-owners
# A dot-path inside the content directories (an editor or agent config) is not content.
/wiki/**/.*         @your-org/vault-owners
/raw/**/.*          @your-org/vault-owners
# Agent harnesses load these as instructions from any directory. make check refuses them
# outside the root and skills/ in any letter case; these lines keep the usual spellings
# owned even so.
**/AGENTS.md            @your-org/vault-owners
**/agents.md            @your-org/vault-owners
**/AGENTS.override.md   @your-org/vault-owners
**/agents.override.md   @your-org/vault-owners
**/CLAUDE.md            @your-org/vault-owners
**/claude.md            @your-org/vault-owners
**/CLAUDE.local.md      @your-org/vault-owners
**/claude.local.md      @your-org/vault-owners
**/GEMINI.md            @your-org/vault-owners
**/gemini.md            @your-org/vault-owners
